# Machine-local settings for SuperMox.
#
# Copy this file to config/local.env and edit the values for your machine.
# config/local.env is git-ignored: it is never committed, so machine-specific
# paths never enter the repository. scripts/local-env.sh sources it (if present)
# and then fills in the portable defaults shown below.
#
# Precedence: exported environment variable > config/local.env > default below.
# So `SUPERMOX_VM_DIR=/some/where bash scripts/vm-start.sh` always wins, and
# `bash scripts/vm-start.sh` alone uses whatever config/local.env says.
#
# Syntax is plain bash assignment; no export keyword needed (local-env.sh exports
# these four itself). scripts/local-env.sh sets REPO (the repo root) before sourcing
# this file, so a value may be written as "$REPO/something" or as an absolute path.

# Where the BUILD VM's disk, kernel and initrd live (scripts/vm-start.sh,
# vm-stop.sh, vm-build-pkg.sh, build-rootfs.sh). Default: inside the repo.
SUPERMOX_VM_DIR="$REPO/build/vm"

# Where the TEST VM's disk lives (scripts/vm-test-install.sh). Always pass
# SUPERMOX_VM_DIR and SUPERMOX_VM_SSH_PORT=2224 together when using the test VM.
SUPERMOX_TEST_DIR="$REPO/build/test-data"

# Where built .deb files are read from (scripts/vm-test-install.sh, build-iso.sh
# uses SUPERMOX_DEBS_DIR too). Default: $SUPERMOX_VM_DIR/debs.
SUPERMOX_DEBS_DIR="$REPO/build/vm/debs"

# Path to a Spaced Linux checkout (git repo) used by scripts/build-iso.sh.
# There is no default that exists on a fresh clone: build-iso.sh stops with a
# clear error naming this variable if the path holds no Spaced checkout.
SUPERMOX_SPACED_REPO="$REPO/../spaced"

# On the maintainer's own machine these point at the data disk (the root disk
# is nearly full), e.g. SUPERMOX_VM_DIR=/media/.../data/supermox-vm; that file
# is kept outside the repo tree and config/local.env is a symlink to it.
